cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Slowest Link or its measurements, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Slowest Link: find recovery promises your system can't keep"
abstract: >-
  Slowest Link checks each recovery promise in a business continuity plan against everything the function depends
  on, declared in the plan, seen in traces and proved by outage tests, and shows the path that breaks it. The plan is
  a Relate by Neo4j graph stored as Markdown notes. Measured on the OpenTelemetry Astronomy Shop 3.1.0 with 1,037
  traces, 20 component stop tests and 14 fault flags, against predictions committed before the tests ran.
authors:
  - family-names: Donovici
    given-names: Marc
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Marc-Dvci/slowest-link"
url: "https://marc-dvci.github.io/slowest-link/"
keywords:
  - business continuity
  - recovery time objective
  - dependency graph
  - OpenTelemetry
  - Relate
  - Neo4j
  - Cypher
  - MCP
